  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">Secure/Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (S/MIME) defined the
Content-Type &quot;application/pkcs7-mime&quot; and the parameter &quot;smime-type&quot;,
along with four valid values for the parameter <xref target="RFC3851" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3851"/>.
Certificate Management over CMS (CMC) added two new parameter values
<xref target="RFC5273" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5273"/>.  <xref target="RFC5751" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5751"/> replaced RFC 3851 and registered the
application/pkcs7-mime media type, but did not create a registry for
the smime-type values.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">Enhanced Security Services for S/MIME <xref target="RFC2634" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2634"/> and Securing X.400
Content with S/MIME <xref target="RFC3854" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3854"/> also add smime-type values.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">When Enrollment over Secure Transport <xref target="RFC7030" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7030"/> added another
parameter value, it became clear that a registry for smime-type
parameter values is necessary.  <xref target="section-2" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Section 2"/> creates this registry,
registers the current values that are defined in previously published
documents, and specifies the policies for registration of new values.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">IANA has changed the reference field for the media type
application/pkcs7-mime to refer to <xref target="RFC5751" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5751"/> and this document.  This document
replaces the references to RFC 5273 and RFC 7030, which are no longer
needed.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-2">IANA has created a new sub-registry under the &quot;MIME Media Type
Sub-Parameter Registries&quot; top-level registry.  The new registry is
&quot;Parameter Values for the smime-type Parameter&quot;, and it references
this document and <xref target="RFC5751" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5751"/>.  The initial values for the registry are
as follows:</t>
      <table align="center" pn="table-1">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">smime-type value</th>
            <th align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">Reference</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">certs-only</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5751" section="3.2.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751#section-3.2.2" derivedContent="RFC5751"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">CMC-Request</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5273" section="3" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5273#section-3" derivedContent="RFC5273"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">CMC-Response</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5273" section="3" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5273#section-3" derivedContent="RFC5273"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">compressed-data</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5751" section="3.2.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751#section-3.2.2" derivedContent="RFC5751"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">enveloped-data</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5751" section="3.2.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751#section-3.2.2" derivedContent="RFC5751"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">enveloped-x400</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC3854" section="3.3.1" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3854#section-3.3.1" derivedContent="RFC3854"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">server-generated-key</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC7030" section="4.4.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7030#section-4.4.2" derivedContent="RFC7030"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">signed-data</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC5751" section="3.2.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751#section-3.2.2" derivedContent="RFC5751"/></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">signed-receipt</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC2634" section="2.4" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2634#section-2.4" derivedContent="RFC2634"/>, bullet 10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">signed-x400</td>
            <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC3854" section="3.2.1" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3854#section-3.2.1" derivedContent="RFC3854"/></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-4">New values can be registered using the Specification Required policy,
as defined in <xref target="RFC5226" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5226"/>.  The S/MIME Message Specification <xref target="RFC5751" section="3.2.2" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751#section-3.2.2" derivedContent="RFC5751"/>, specifies guidelines for assigning new smime-type
parameter values, and those guidelines apply to the assignment of
values in this registry.</t>
    </section>
